thcal L_k\\).\n\nThus every point of \\(T_n\\) is covered by at least one line of \\(\\mathcal L_k\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nFor each integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) and each integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n-2\\) we have exhibited an explicit set of \\(n\\) distinct lines that\n\n* covers every lattice point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge 1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\), and\n* contains exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\nHence all integers \\(k\\) in the interval \\(\\{0,1,\\dots ,n-2\\}\\) are admissible.  \nThe status of the two remaining values \\(k=n-1\\) and \\(k=n\\) is not settled by the present argument.\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
